// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-05 | Modified: 2026-11-05
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.002
// Description: Detects usage of the Quarks PwDump tool via commandline arguments
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/quarkslab/quarkspwdump
//   - https://symantec-enterprise-blogs.security.com/blogs/threat-intelligence/seedworm-apt-iran-middle-east
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6a30e3674e4b3f048b7d8fbd3dafab5e5d3bf22f/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_quarks_pwdump.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\QuarksPwDump.exe" or (ProcessCommandLine contains " -dhl" or ProcessCommandLine contains " --dump-hash-local" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -dhdc" or ProcessCommandLine contains " --dump-hash-domain-cached" or ProcessCommandLine contains " --dump-bitlocker" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -dhd " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --dump-hash-domain " or ProcessCommandLine contains "--ntds-file")
